export anchor CashRegisterStyle:
    number: 164
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Cash register
    idea: The dashboard is a point-of-sale terminal, with green LCD windows ringing up the totals, projects as item lines on the sale screen, the menu as a block of chunky department keys and activity printed on a journal tape.
    base: light
    palette:
        counter: #e9e4d8, the page behind the terminal
        case: #f8f5ee, the terminal body and the style sheet
        caseEdge: #a89f8c, the case border, never text
        lcd: #cbd8bb, every display window and the search field
        lcdInk: #1c2a12, all text and bars on the LCD
        keyCream: #fffdf6, department keys and secondary keys
        keyNavy: #1f3a5f, the New project key and the sale screen title bar
        ink: #23201b, text on paper and on cream keys
        muted: #5b5446, PLU codes, departments and small labels
        green: #24602f, the On track code with a circle check
        amber: #8a4f00, the At risk code with a triangle
        voidRed: #9e2121, the Behind code with a crossed square and the notice count
        focusBlue: #1f5fd1, the focus outline only
    type:
        Two stacks. LCD and receipt text use Consolas, DejaVu Sans Mono,
        Menlo, Liberation Mono, monospace in bold caps. Keys use Arial
        Black, Helvetica Neue, Arial in 900 weight caps. Totals are 44px
        mono, the LCD greeting 26px mono caps, key labels 13 to 20px,
        item lines and tape 13 to 14px mono, and small labels 11px mono
        caps tracked 0.12em. The clerk name is 15px system-ui.
    layout:
        One rounded cream terminal case holds everything. Across the top a
        pole display shows the brand at left, a wide LCD in the middle with
        Good morning, Mara and the date plus an octagon Overdue 4 tasks
        line, and the clerk name at right. Below are four LCD windows for
        the totals, each with a small window number. The left column is a
        white sale screen with a navy title bar and a table of item lines
        with PLU, item, department, quantity done over total, percent with
        a ticked bar, due date and a status code, ending in a subtotal row.
        The right column is the keypad, with six department keys D1 to D6
        for the nav, Home pressed down and tinted yellow, a PLU lookup LCD
        search field, Notices and clerk keys and a full-width New project
        key. Under both sits a white journal tape with a zigzag torn top
        listing activity, beside an LCD Z report bar chart of daily tasks
        closed. Below 960px the keypad drops under the sale screen and the
        tape stacks above the chart. The table scrolls sideways inside its
        screen on phones.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px inside the case and between blocks, 8px between keys.
    density: Busy and tactile like a shop counter. Many small windows, every key large enough for a thumb.
    corners: 18px on the case, 8px on keys and LCD bezels, 4px on status codes.
    borders: A 6px dark bezel round each LCD, 2px taupe key edges, dashed rules between item lines and tape entries, a 2px rule above the subtotal.
    shadows: Keys stand on a hard 4px bottom ledge and the current key is pressed down to 1px. LCDs have an inset shadow. The case has a 6px ledge and a soft drop.
    icons:
        Solid geometric marks at text size. A circle with a check for On
        track, a triangle with a bang for At risk, a square with a cross
        for Behind and an octagon with a bang for Overdue, always beside a
        caps word inside a bordered code box. Chart bars are made of
        stacked LCD segments.
    focus: A 3px focus blue outline offset 3px on keys, fields and rows.
    tone: Register shorthand in caps, such as Item lines, Subtotal, PLU lookup, Journal tape and Z report.
